.TH GGE\-SCENES 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-scenes \- how scenes and the scene stack work
.SH DESCRIPTION
A scene is one mode of the game: title, gameplay, pause, inventory, dialog.
It is a
.B Scene
struct holding up to five callbacks and two flags:
.nf
.ft B
typedef struct Scene {
  const char *name;
  void (*on_enter)(Engine *, Scene *);
  void (*on_exit)(Engine *, Scene *);
  void (*handle_input)(Engine *, Scene *, const Input *);
  void (*update)(Engine *, Scene *, float dt);
  void (*render)(Engine *, Scene *, float alpha);
  bool blocks_update_below;
  bool blocks_render_below;
} Scene;
.ft R
.fi
NULL callbacks are skipped. Each scene is a singleton: a static
.B Scene
inside a getter such as
.BR title_scene() ,
which returns its address.
.SS The stack
The engine keeps a stack of at most 8 scenes.
.BR engine_push (3),
.BR engine_pop (3)
and
.BR engine_replace (3)
queue changes that are applied after the current callback returns, so a scene
may pop itself from its own handle_input. The loop ends when the stack empties
or
.BR engine_quit (3)
is called.
.SS Per-frame order
.IP 1. 3
.B handle_input
on the top scene only.
.IP 2. 3
Queued stack changes applied.
.IP 3. 3
.B update(dt)
zero or more times at the fixed tick rate, walking down from the top and
stopping after the first scene whose
.B blocks_update_below
is true.
.IP 4. 3
Queued stack changes applied.
.IP 5. 3
.B render(alpha)
once, from the lowest scene whose
.B blocks_render_below
is true up to the top.
.SS The two flags
.TS
l l l.
update	render	use
true	true	title, game over, gameplay itself
true	false	pause menu, dialog, confirm, shop
false	false	HUD, toast, minimap
.TE
.SS on_enter / on_exit
.B on_enter
runs when the scene actually lands on the stack; reset scene\-private
statics, load assets, build menus, snap the camera.
.B on_exit
runs when it leaves, by pop, replace, or shutdown; free sounds, stop music,
turn off text input.
.SS alpha
.B render
receives how far the simulation is between the last tick and the next, 0..1.
Draw moving things at
.BR v2_lerp "(prev, now, alpha)"
so motion is smooth above the tick rate. It has nothing to do with
transparency.
.SS Passing data to a scene
Give the scene an opener that stores what it needs in a static and pushes:
.nf
.ft B
static int target;
void shop_scene_open(Engine *e, int cat) { target = cat; engine_push(e, shop_scene()); }
.ft R
.fi
Store indices, never pointers into GameState; a loaded save moves the data.
